<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place</p><h1 class="enc-title">Croatia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Croatia is a country in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> on the eastern Adriatic coast, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagreb">Zagreb</a>. A medieval Croatian duchy became a kingdom around 925 and in 1102 entered a union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> that lasted, under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> rule from 1527, until 1918. After belonging to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslavia</a> it declared independence in 1991, fought the Croatian War of Independence, and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a> in 2013.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/croatia.jpg" alt="Croatia" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nightstallion, Elephantus, Neoneo13, Denelson83, Rainman, R-41, Minestrone, Lupo, Zscout370,MaGa (based on Decision o... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Croatia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
